        <section id="impact" class="reading-section">
          <h2>Impact and afterlife</h2>

          <p>
            The original Transformer is an encoder-decoder translation model. Modern LLMs usually use only part of that
            template. <button class="anno" data-anno="bert">BERT</button> is encoder-only and emphasizes understanding.
            <button class="anno" data-anno="gpt">GPT</button> is decoder-only and emphasizes next-token generation.
            <button class="anno" data-anno="chatgpt">ChatGPT</button> is not simply “the Transformer paper turned into a product”;
            it is a later stack of scale, pretraining, instruction tuning, feedback learning, safety work, and interface design.
          </p>

          <div class="results-table-wrap">
            <table class="results-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Period</th>
                  <th>What changed</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
